// Out-of-thin-air through a numeric fixpoint rather than a load-buffering cycle.
//
// Source: the MRD line's numbered out-of-thin-air listings.
//
// x = y + z, y = x / 2 and z = x / 2, so x = x/2 + x/2 holds for any x and the
// value is pinned by nothing but the cycle through it. The asserted outcome is
// stronger than that: @x = 42 forces y = z = 21, while @y = @z = 42 forces
// x = 84, so it is unreachable arithmetically as well as by dependency.
//
// The forbid had a witness (#41) for neither reason. @x was the *location*
// variable rather than the final value at it -- the lexer bound '@x' with the
// '@' still attached, so it never matched the memory state's key -- and the
// three locations were free symbols the solver could set to 42. See #84.
x := 2; y := 1; z := 1;
{
  r0 := y;
  r1 := z;
  r2 := r0 + r1;
  x := r2
}|||{
  r3 := x;
  y := r3 / 2
}|||{
  r4 := x;
  z := r4 / 2
}
%% forbid (@x = 42 && @y = 42 && @z = 42) []
